         <div type="bio">
            <p>American writer, journalist, editor, and model. Foster was the companion of New York lawyer and art patron <name type="person" key="quin70">John Quinn</name> from 1918 until his death in 1924. She knew and corresponded with many writers and authors, including <name type="person" key="ID_MISSING">John Butler Yeats</name>, <name type="person" key="yeat65">W.B. Yeats</name>, <name type="person" key="poun85">Ezra Pound</name>, <name type="person" key="ford73">Ford Madox Ford</name>, <name type="person" key="ID_MISSING">Picasso</name>, and <name type="person" key="ID_MISSING">Constantin Brancusi</name>. Foster was assistant editor of the <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">American Review of Reviews</name>, and in 1924 also American editor of Ford Madox Ford’s <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Transatlantic Review</name> when the first installment of JJ’s “Work in Progress” appeared. She wrote and published books of narrative verse and volumes of stories. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
